Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-10-2000||10:55 PM||||Well, it seems I have the problem that lots of others do, but I have never seen a straight answer.. I have to crank the engine for like 10-15 seconds before it starts cold. (It usually stalls a second after that and then doing it again it will run fine)... Also, sometimes when it's reved and I let go of the gas, the rpm's drop to about 600-700... Now, is it the ignition coil I have to replace? (I need to know before I go through the pain of installing this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It is a 4cyl 85se.. Thanks!||||reg||4
Z||000001||theogre||04-11-2000||10:16 AM||||not likely the coil.<P>check static timing.<P>put a scanner on it and read the sensors. one of them may be getting cruddy.<P>check the oil pressure and check/replace the oil presure sender. If oil pressure is slow coming up or the OP switch is lagging then it can crank awhile. Oil pressure sender runs the fuel pump as well. (The ECM only runs it for 5 sec.)||||reg||1
